-- title:
--   Integral closedness of R'⊗_ℤ_{(ℓ)}chartAlgFin for a DVR base
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $N \neq 0$ and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$, and write $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ for the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt ℓ`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of those rationals whose denominator is coprime to $\ell$. Let $A =$ `chartAlgFin N ℓ` be the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-subalgebra of the field $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldFull N` whose elements are those integral over the subalgebra $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}[j]$ generated by the element `jFull N`. Let $R'$ be a commutative ring which is a domain and a discrete valuation ring, equipped with a $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-algebra structure and with residue field `IsLocalRing.ResidueField R'` of characteristic $\ell$, and let $K'$ be a field which is a fraction field of $R'$, carrying a $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-algebra structure compatible with that of $R'$ via a scalar tower. Assume that the generic fibre $K' \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}} A$ is a domain and is integrally closed (in its field of fractions). The conclusion is that $R' \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}} A$ is likewise a domain and is integrally closed.
--
--   This is the descent step along a discrete valuation base for the $j$-finite chart of the Igusa integral model: integral closedness of the chart over a local base is deduced from integral closedness of its generic fibre together with reducedness of the fibre in characteristic $\ell$, the situation of good reduction at primes $\ell \nmid N$. It is used in the construction of an injective algebra map out of the tensor product of a chart algebra with integrally closed target, [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.exists_algHom_tensor_chartAlg_injective_isIntegrallyClosed`](thm.html#ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.exists_algHom_tensor_chartAlg_injective_isIntegrallyClosed).
